/F1 10 Tf
11.5 TL
0 g
56.6929133858267775 785.1970866141732586 Td
(GrainFlow uses Supabase Auth with server-side rendering \(SSR\). Key security properties:) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 10 Tf
11.5 TL
0 g
56.6929133858267775 756.8506299212598378 Td
(  - Session management: Auth sessions are stored in HttpOnly cookies, not localStorage. This prevents) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 10 Tf
11.5 TL
0 g
56.6929133858267775 742.6774015748030706 Td
(JavaScript-based session theft \(XSS attacks\).) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 10 Tf
11.5 TL
0 g
56.6929133858267775 722.8348818897637784 Td
(  - CSRF protection: Built into the Supabase SSR auth flow.) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 10 Tf
11.5 TL
0 g
56.6929133858267775 702.9923622047243725 Td
(  - Server-side verification: Every server action re-verifies the user's auth session before processing. There is) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 10 Tf
11.5 TL
0 g
56.6929133858267775 688.819133858267719 Td
(no trust of client-side session claims.) Tj
ET
BT
/F2 11 Tf
12.6499999999999986 TL
0 g
56.6929133858267775 654.8033858267716596 Td
(Session Flow) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 10 Tf
11.5 TL
0 g
56.6929133858267775 625.0396062992125508 Td
(  1. User submits credentials to Supabase Auth.) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 10 Tf
11.5 TL
0 g
56.6929133858267775 605.1970866141732586 Td
(  2. Supabase returns a session token stored in an HttpOnly cookie.) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 10 Tf
11.5 TL
0 g
56.6929133858267775 585.3545669291338527 Td
(  3. On each server action call, the server reads the cookie, verifies the token with Supabase, and retrieves) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 10 Tf
11.5 TL
0 g
56.6929133858267775 571.1813385826771992 Td
(the current user.) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 10 Tf
11.5 TL
0 g
56.6929133858267775 551.3388188976377933 Td
(  4. If the token is invalid or expired, the user is redirected to /login.) Tj
ET
BT
/F2 14 Tf
16.0999999999999979 TL
0 g
56.6929133858267775 514.4884251968503577 Td
(RBAC Enforcement) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 10 Tf
11.5 TL
0 g
56.6929133858267775 474.8033858267716028 Td
(Role-Based Access Control is enforced at three layers, as described in Chapter 22. From a security) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 10 Tf
11.5 TL
0 g
56.6929133858267775 460.6301574803148924 Td
(perspective:) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 10 Tf
11.5 TL
0 g
56.6929133858267775 432.2837007874015285 Td
(  1. UI layer hides controls but is not a security boundary \(can be bypassed with browser dev tools\).) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 10 Tf
11.5 TL
0 g
56.6929133858267775 412.4411811023621226 Td
(  2. Server action layer is the primary enforcement point. Every 'use server' function checks the user's role) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 10 Tf
11.5 TL
0 g
56.6929133858267775 398.2679527559054691 Td
(before performing operations.) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 10 Tf
11.5 TL
0 g
56.6929133858267775 378.4254330708660632 Td
(  3. Database layer \(RLS\) is the last line of defense, ensuring data access is constrained even if the server) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 10 Tf
11.5 TL
0 g
56.6929133858267775 364.2522047244094097 Td
(action layer has a bug.) Tj
ET
BT
/F2 11 Tf
12.6499999999999986 TL
0 g
56.6929133858267775 330.2364566929132934 Td
(The authenticatedAction Pattern) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 10 Tf
11.5 TL
0 g
56.6929133858267775 300.4726771653542983 Td
(Many server actions use a wrapper function called authenticatedAction that:) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 10 Tf
11.5 TL
0 g
56.6929133858267775 272.1262204724408775 Td
(  1. Retrieves the current user from the auth session.) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 10 Tf
11.5 TL
0 g
56.6929133858267775 252.2837007874014716 Td
(  2. Fetches the user's profile and role.) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 10 Tf
11.5 TL
0 g
56.6929133858267775 232.4411811023621794 Td
(  3. Passes the verified user, Supabase client, and role to the action handler.) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 10 Tf
11.5 TL
0 g
56.6929133858267775 212.5986614173227736 Td
(  4. Returns an error if authentication fails.) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 10 Tf
11.5 TL
0 g
56.6929133858267775 184.2522047244093528 Td
(This centralizes auth checking and prevents individual actions from forgetting to verify the session.) Tj
ET
BT
/F2 14 Tf
16.0999999999999979 TL
0 g
56.6929133858267775 147.4018110236219172 Td
(Audit Trail) Tj
